r is burning while white smoke is emitting from it.\n","first_frame":"assets/0f5ce8b3a8339094dd1c.png","source_video":null,"candidates":[],"events":[{"kind":"command_execution","utc":"2026-11-10T07:13:31.124244+00:00","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'ls -la && cat prompt.txt && cat GENERATION_RULES.md'","aggregated_output":"total 88\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 tiger tiger  4096 Nov 10 15:13 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 tiger tiger  4096 Nov 10 15:13 ..\ndr-xr-xr-x 2 tiger tiger    40 Nov 10 15:13 .agents\ndr-xr-xr-x 2 tiger tiger    40 Nov 10 15:13 .aws\ndr-xr-xr-x 2 tiger tiger    40 Nov 10 15:13 .codex\ndr-xr-xr-x 2 tiger tiger    40 Nov 10 15:13 .git\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 tiger tiger  4096 Nov 10 15:12 .tmp\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 tiger tiger   941 Nov  9 12:30 GENERATION_RULES.md\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 tiger tiger  4026 Nov  9 12:30 artifact_io.py\n-rw-r--r-- 1 tiger tiger 59163 Oct 30 19:21 first_frame.png\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 tiger tiger  3262 Nov  9 12:30 player_template.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 tiger tiger   347 Oct 30 19:21 prompt.txt\nStatic locked-off single-shot with fixed frame throughout filmed with constant framerate in real-time. The scene shows a realistic scientific demonstration. The scene only contains the described setup and actions. The piece of folded paper sits on a glass cutting board. The piece of folded paper is burning while white smoke is emitting from it.\n# PixelWorld generation contract v2\n\n- Use only `first_frame.png` and `prompt.txt`. Work inside this workspace. No network, other cases, reference continuations, masks, scores, memory, external AI models, learned weights, external simulation/rendering engines, or subagents.\n- Generate 20 RGB frames at 256×144, 4 fps, for 5 seconds. Frame 00 must be pixel-identical to `first_frame.png`.\n- Implement `generate.py` and call `artifact_io.save(frames, case_dir)` with uint8 RGB arrays of shape `(20,144,256,3)`. Keep `generate.py` runnable so it regenerates the submitted RGB video. Local Python drawing, image operations, shading, analytic geometry and mathematical dynamics are allowed.\n- Choose your own approach and use the tools permitted by your Track. Save intermediate generated results in the workspace when producing candidates for inspection.\n- Use `.tmp/` for temporary files. No additional planning or method report is required.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"},{"kind":"command_execution","utc":"2026-11-10T07:13:36.523162+00:00","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat artifact_io.py && cat player_template.html && python3 -c \\\"\nfrom PIL import Image\nimport numpy as np\nim = Image.open('first_frame.png')\nprint(im.size, im.mode)\na = np.array(im)\nprint(a.shape, a.dtype)\nprint(a.min(), a.max())\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Output-only helpers. No drawing or generation policy is implemented here.\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport base64\nimport json\nimport wave\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw\n\n\ndef save(frames, case_dir, audio=None):\n    case_dir = Path(case_dir)\n    frames = np.asarray(frames)\n    path = case_dir / \"task_spec.json\"\n    spec = json.loads(path.read_text()) if path.is_file() else {}\n    n, h, w, fps = (spec.get(\"frames\", 20), spec.get(\"height\", 144), spec.get(\"width\", 256), spec.get(\"fps\", 4))\n    assert frames.shape == (n, h, w, 3) and frames.dtype == np.uint8, frames.shape\n    audio_spec = spec.get(\"audio\")\n    audio_url = None\n    if audio_spec:\n        samples = round(n / fps * audio_spec[\"sample_rate\"])\n        pcm = np.asarray(audio)\n        if pcm.ndim == 1:\n            pcm = pcm[:, None]\n        assert pcm.shape == (samples, audio_spec[\"channels\"]) and pcm.dtype == np.int16, (pcm.shape, pcm.dtype)\n        with wave.open(str(case_dir / \"audio.wav\"), \"wb\") as handle:\n            handle.setnchannels(audio_spec[\"channels\"])\n            handle.setsampwidth(2)\n            handle.setframerate(audio_spec[\"sample_rate\"])\n            handle.writeframes(pcm.astype(\"<i2\").tobytes())\n        audio_url = \"data:audio/wav;base64,\" + base64.b64encode((case_dir / \"audio.wav\").read_bytes()).decode()\n    values = frames.astype(np.uint32)\n    packed = (values[:, :, :, 0] << 16) | (values[:, :, :, 1] << 8) | values[:, :, :, 2]\n    tensor = packed.transpose(1, 2, 0)\n    np.savez_compressed(case_dir / \"pixels.npz\", pixels=tensor)\n\n    folder = case_dir / \"frames\"\n    folder.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    for index, frame in enumerate(frames):\n        Image.fromarray(frame).save(folder / f\"{index:02d}.png\")\n\n    sheet = Image.new(\"RGB\", (w * 4, (h + 21) * 2), (25, 28, 35))\n    draw = ImageDraw.Draw(sheet)\n    for index, frame_index in enumerate(np.linspace(0, n - 1, 8).round().astype(int)):\n        x, y = (index % 4) * w, (index // 4) * (h + 21)\n        draw.text((x + 5, y + 3), f\"frame {frame_index:02d} · {frame_index / fps:.2f}s\", fill=\"white\")\n        sheet.paste(Image.fromarray(frames[frame_index]), (x, y + 21))\n    sheet.save(case_dir / \"inspection.png\")\n\n    transition = Image.new(\"RGB\", (w * 4, h * 2 + 21), (25, 28, 35))\n    draw = ImageDraw.Draw(transition)\n    for index, frame_index in enumerate(min(i, n-1) for i in range(4)):\n        x = index * w\n        draw.text((x + 5, 4), f\"frame {frame_index:02d} · {frame_index / fps:.2f}s\", fill=\"white\")\n        transition.paste(Image.fromarray(frames[frame_index]), (x, 21))\n        transition.paste(Image.fromarray(frames[frame_index]).resize((w, h), Image.Resampling.NEAREST), (x, h + 21))\n    transition.save(case_dir / \"transition_check.png\")\n\n    encode = lambda array: base64.b64encode(np.asarray(array, dtype=\"<u4\").tobytes()).decode()\n    deltas = []\n    for index in range(1, n):\n        current = packed[index].reshape(-1)\n        previous = packed[index - 1].reshape(-1)\n        positions = np.flatnonzero(current != previous)\n        packet = []\n        if len(positions):\n            bounds = np.r_[0, np.flatnonzero(np.diff(positions) > 1) + 1, len(positions)]\n            for start, end in zip(bounds[:-1], bounds[1:]):\n                offset = int(positions[start])\n                count = int(end - start)\n                packet.extend([offset, count])\n                packet.extend(current[offset:offset + count].tolist())\n        deltas.append(encode(packet))\n    data = {\n        \"id\": case_dir.name,\n        \"width\": w, \"height\": h, \"frames\": n, \"fps\": fps, \"audio\": audio_url,\n        \"first\": encode(packed[0].reshape(-1)),\n        \"deltas\": deltas,\n        \"caption\": (case_dir / \"prompt.txt\").read_text().strip(),\n    }\n    template = (Path(__file__).parent / \"player_template.html\").read_text()\n    payload = json.dumps(data, separators=(\",\", \":\"), ensure_ascii=False).replace(\"<\", \"\\\\u003c\")\n    (case_dir / \"index.html\").write_text(template.replace(\"__ID__\", case_dir.name).replace(\"__DATA__\", payload))\n<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<title>PixelWorld · __ID__</title><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;padding:16px;background:#101419;color:#eef3f7;font:14px system-ui,sans-serif}canvas{display:block;width:min(100%,768px);height:auto;image-rendering:pixelated;background:#080a0c;border-radius:8px;margin:auto}.controls{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;max-width:768px;margin:14px auto 0}button{background:#a5ef83;border:0;border-radius:7px;color:#142110;padding:9px 16px;font:inherit;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}input[type=range]{flex:1;min-width:100px}.caption{max-width:768px;margin:12px auto;color:#a7b0be;font-size:12px;line-height:1.5}</style>\n<canvas id=\"canvas\" width=\"256\" height=\"144\"></canvas><div class=\"controls\"><button id=\"play\">Play</button><button id=\"replay\">Replay</button><input id=\"seek\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"19\" value=\"0\"><output id=\"time\"></output><label><input id=\"loop\" type=\"checkbox\" checked> Loop</label></div><div id=\"caption\" class=\"caption\"></div>\n<script>'use strict';const DATA=__DATA__,W=DATA.width||256,H=DATA.height||144,N=DATA.frames||20,FPS=DATA.fps||4;function unpack(s){const t=atob(s),b=new Uint8Array(t.length);for(let i=0;i<t.length;i++)b[i]=t.charCodeAt(i);return new Uint32Array(b.buffer)}const frames=[unpack(DATA.first)];for(const encoded of DATA.deltas){const f=new Uint32Array(frames.at(-1)),p=unpack(encoded);for(let i=0;i<p.length;){const start=p[i++],count=p[i++];f.set(p.subarray(i,i+count),start);i+=count}frames.push(f)}const canvas=document.getElementById('canvas'),ctx=canvas.getContext('2d');canvas.width=W;canvas.height=H;const img=ctx.createImageData(W,H);seek.max=N-1;const audio=DATA.audio?new Audio(DATA.audio):null;let frame=0,playing=false,raf=null,started=0;function draw(n){frame=Math.max(0,Math.min(N-1,n));const pixels=frames[frame];for(let i=0;i<pixels.length;i++){const v=pixels[i],p=i*4;img.data[p]=v>>>16;img.data[p+1]=(v>>>8)&255;img.data[p+2]=v&255;img.data[p+3]=255}ctx.putImageData(img,0,0);seek.value=frame;time.textContent=`${frame+1}/${N} · ${(frame/FPS).toFixed(2)} / ${(N/FPS).toFixed(2)}s`}function pause(){playing=false;cancelAnimationFrame(raf);if(audio)audio.pause();play.textContent='Play'}function tick(t){if(!playing)return;let elapsed=audio?audio.currentTime:(t-started)/1000;if(elapsed>=N/FPS){if(loop.checked){started=t;if(audio){audio.currentTime=0;audio.play()}elapsed=0}else{draw(N-1);pause();return}}draw(Math.min(N-1,Math.floor(elapsed*FPS)));raf=requestAnimationFrame(tick)}async function start(){if(playing)return;if(frame===N-1)draw(0);started=performance.now()-frame/FPS*1000;if(audio){audio.currentTime=frame/FPS;try{await audio.play()}catch(e){caption.textContent='Audio playback failed: '+e.message;return}}playing=true;play.textContent='Pause';raf=requestAnimationFrame(tick)}play.onclick=()=>playing?pause():start();replay.onclick=()=>{pause();draw(0);start()};seek.oninput=e=>{pause();draw(+e.target.value)};caption.textContent=DATA.caption+(audio?' · RGB + PCM audio':'');if(audio)audio.onended=()=>{if(playing&&loop.checked){audio.currentTime=0;audio.play()}else pause()};draw(0);window.__pixelReady=true;</script></html>\n(256, 144) RGB\n(144, 256, 3) uint8\n17 255\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"},{"kind":"agent_message","utc":"2026-11-10T07:13:48.547758+00:00","text":"Let me analyze the first frame numerically to understand the scene layout, since I can't view it directly.\n"},{"kind":"command_execution","utc":"2026-11-10T07:13:49.855630+00:00","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd [workspace path] && python3 << 'EOF'\nimport numpy as np\nfrom PIL import Image\na = np.array(Image.open('first_frame.png')).astype(int)\nh,w,_ = a.shape\n# coarse 32x18 grid of average colors\nfor y in range(0,h,8):\n    row=[]\n    for x in range(0,w,8):\n        block = a[y:y+8,x:x+8].mean(axis=(0,1)).astype(int)\n        row.append(f\\\"{block[0]:3d},{block[1]:3d},{block[2]:3d}\\\")\n    print(\\\" \\\".join(row))\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":" 71, 72,104  93, 92,124  76, 69, 78  75, 67, 73  82, 75, 84  91, 87,101 103,105,125 115,124,150 120,130,157 116,122,146 121,120,135 114,111,131  96, 91,104  93, 87,105  94, 90,112  95, 91,117  89, 83,102  93, 86,100  95, 89,102  95, 90,103  97, 91,104  96, 92,105  95, 91,104  90, 86,100  89, 84, 98  83, 78, 93  77, 71, 88  68, 62, 80  66, 60, 84  69, 67, 96  71, 70,102  64, 62, 90\n 63, 52, 50  65, 54, 54  68, 59, 60  71, 63, 68  76, 70, 75  84, 79, 88  94, 92,106 103,105,126 107,113,137 101,104,125  99, 97,113 104,101,119  97, 92,107  90, 85,102  92, 89,110  98, 94,122  94, 87,103  91, 84, 96  93, 85, 97  94, 87, 98  93, 86, 98  91, 84, 96  87, 80, 92  87, 80, 92  86, 80, 91  86, 80, 91  83, 77, 87  74, 67, 74  62, 54, 57  56, 48, 52  52, 43, 52  50, 41, 55\n 62, 51, 48  64, 54, 52  66, 57, 56  69, 62, 64  75, 67, 72  80, 75, 80  88, 84, 94  95, 93,108  94, 94,112  92, 90,110  83, 80, 94  85, 81,100  92, 86,104  91, 84,101  95, 89,107 101, 98,122  95, 88,106  92, 84, 93  93, 